From e37b706f80eab7afb14897ef1e8a710ea44a0bd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:06:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zeo_i18n, settings_ui: the Language page marks a translation
 nobody native reviewed

0194-0202 ship eight translations drafted with Lara and revised by the agent; none has been
reviewed by a native speaker (docs/assets/zeo-i18n-0194-0202-2026-11-26/README.md lists the
known faults). The operator chose to release them all with that said on screen (2026-11-26),
so a person picking "Deutsch" knows it is a draft before trusting a label.

The mark lives in the translation itself: a language's own zeo.ftl carries
zeo-language-machine-translated, read like zeo-language-name from that language's bundle
alone, so English never lends it and a fallback never hides it. A native reviewer deletes the
line and the mark is gone; no code, list or patch has to change. es, fr, it, de, ru, ja and
zh-CN carry it; pt-BR does not -- it shipped in 0.28.0 and its review is the operator's.

The picker shows "Deutsch (machine translation)" with the suffix in the language the UI is in
now, since that is the one the person choosing can read. The trigger shows the same label, so
the choice stays visible after it is made.

i18n-check.py learns that the mark exists only in translations (TRANSLATION_ONLY): English
lacking it is not staleness.

Ungrouped, after 0202: it touches only 0177/0194's files and the language directories.
